            "John Quincy Adams became the sixth President in 1825, making the Adamses the first father-son presidential pair."),
        q("a20", "adams", "What was the name of the Adams family home in Quincy, Massachusetts?",
            listOf("Peacefield", "Monticello", "Montpelier", "Mount Vernon"), 0,
            "Adams named his Quincy estate 'Peacefield,' reflecting his hope for peace after decades of public service."),
        q("a21", "adams", "Adams helped write the 1780 constitution of which state, still the oldest continuously functioning written constitution in the world?",
            listOf("Massachusetts", "Virginia", "Pennsylvania", "New York"), 0,
            "Adams was the primary author of the Massachusetts Constitution of 1780, a model for the later U.S. Constitution."),
        q("a22", "adams", "Adams's 1776 pamphlet 'Thoughts on Government' influenced many states by recommending what structure?",
            listOf("A single all-powerful legislature", "Separation of powers among three branches of government", "Rule by a council of elders", "Direct democracy with no representatives"), 1,
            "Adams argued for separated powers and checks and balances, ideas that shaped several state constitutions."),
        q("a23", "adams", "On what date did Adams die, coincidentally the same day as Thomas Jefferson and the Declaration's 50th anniversary?",
            listOf("July 4, 1826", "December 14, 1799", "April 17, 1790", "June 28, 1836"), 0,
            "Adams died July 4, 1826, hours after Jefferson, exactly fifty years after the Declaration of Independence was adopted."),
        q("a24", "adams", "In his final years, Adams resumed a famous, warm correspondence with which former rival?",
            listOf("Thomas Jefferson", "Alexander Hamilton", "Aaron Burr", "George III"), 0,
            "After years of political estrangement, Adams and Jefferson exchanged over a decade of thoughtful letters before both died in 1826."),
        q("a25", "adams", "Before the Revolutionary War, Adams served in the Continental Congress, where he nominated whom to command the new Continental Army?",
            listOf("George Washington", "Nathanael Greene", "Horatio Gates", "Benedict Arnold"), 0,
            "Adams nominated Washington as commander-in-chief in 1775, a choice that helped unify the colonies behind the war effort."),
        q("a26", "adams", "Adams was the first President to reside in what building, though it was still unfinished when he moved in during 1800?",
            listOf("The White House", "Independence Hall", "Federal Hall", "Monticello"), 0,
            "Adams became the first President to live in the White House, moving to the then-unfinished building in Washington, D.C., in 1800."),
        q("a27", "adams", "Which political stance best describes Adams's early position on independence, before he became one of its leading advocates?",
            listOf("He was initially cautious, favoring efforts at reconciliation with Britain", "He never supported independence at all", "He supported independence from childhood", "He wanted to remain a British colony permanently"), 0,
            "Like many delegates, Adams initially hoped for reconciliation before concluding that independence was necessary."),
        q("a28", "adams", "Adams was a member of which political party, generally favoring a stronger federal government?",
            listOf("The Federalist Party", "The Anti-Federalist Party", "The Democratic-Republican Party", "The Whig Party"), 0,
            "Adams aligned with the Federalists, though he often charted his own independent course within the party."),
        q("a29", "adams", "What did Adams consider his proudest achievement as President, even though it cost him political support and re-election?",
            listOf("Avoiding a full-scale war with France", "Signing the Alien and Sedition Acts", "The Louisiana Purchase", "Winning the War of 1812"), 0,
            "Adams later said keeping the peace with France, despite the political cost, was his greatest presidential achievement."),
        q("a30", "adams", "Before serving as President, Adams also served as U.S. minister (ambassador) to which country, securing an important loan and recognition?",
            listOf("The Netherlands", "Spain", "Prussia", "Russia"), 0,
            "Adams served as America's first minister to the Netherlands, securing crucial loans and diplomatic recognition for the new nation."),
        q("a31", "adams", "How did Adams actually respond when Abigail urged him to 'remember the ladies' while drafting new laws in 1776?",
            listOf("He treated her request lightly and did not push for legal changes to women's status", "He immediately proposed giving women the vote", "He resigned in protest of women's treatment", "He asked Congress to make Abigail a delegate"), 0,
            "Despite valuing Abigail's political judgment privately, Adams brushed off her request in his reply, and no legal changes for women followed."),
        q("a32", "adams", "Read this excerpt from Abigail Adams's 1776 letter to her husband. What is she most directly asking for?",
            listOf("Legal protections for women against unlimited power by their husbands", "The right to serve in Congress herself", "Full military conscription for women", "A ban on all future taxation"), 0,
            "Abigail Adams asked that new laws 'remember the ladies' and not give husbands unlimited power over their wives — an early, notable call for women's legal protections.",
            stimulus = "\"...in the new Code of Laws... I desire you would Remember the Ladies, and be more generous and favourable to them than your ancestors. Do not put such unlimited power into the hands of the Husbands.\" — Abigail Adams, letter to John Adams, March 31, 1776")
    )

